@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@
+# Isolated deterministic owner-admission prerequisite
+
+Astra authorization: OWNER_ADMISSION_DESIGN_APPROVED_FOR_DETERMINISTIC_IMPLEMENTATION.
+
+Stage E RED; Stage F NOT STARTED; PAPER ONLY. Material budget remains 6/6 consumed, 0 unused.
+
+Before implementing the approved gate, retain the required real interruption/completion assertion against the pinned production runtime. An actual priority-0 owner request arrives during the native completion ledger query, after a real bounded 512-record archive slice. The existing 1,000-VM SQL interruption handler, ordinary Runtime.turn(), arbiter, ledger, durable episode and accepted futures remain unmodified. No expectedFailure, skips, manual completion, pending reset or M1 repair is permitted.
+
+One finite fixture: 128 archived seed records in valid account scopes plus 1,800 hot program records, one native immutable 1,000-record archive receipt and two ordinary maintenance submissions. No source stream, provider access, cadence simulation, capacity/pressure cohort, qualification or material run. A trace callback positions real urgent arrival; it does not raise, replace SQL or alter the progress interval.
+
+If this required prerequisite fails with the M1 in-flight decision blocker, stop implementation and preserve complete evidence for Astra. The approved gate and its full deterministic matrix are not represented as implemented or passed.
+
+The dedicated workflow runs only this prerequisite and saves its raw evidence. The existing broad push job is suppressed through its preexisting [runtime-v2-promotion] message guard; no production promotion is invoked. All preexisting source, workflows, tests, evidence and housekeeping patch files retain their exact blobs and modes. The housekeeping correctness patch remains stored separately and is not applied here.
